# LF everywhere, in the repo and in every checkout.
#
# scripts/docs-switcher.ts decides drift by string equality, so a CRLF working tree
# (git's default on Windows) would report all 16 READMEs as drifted, block every commit
# through the pre-commit hook, and stay invisible in CI — which runs on ubuntu.
# The .githooks/ shell scripts need LF to be runnable at all.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.gif binary
